B.B3=new A.as(B.Br,["Hello, engineer!","Hello, {n}!","Quick start","Appearance","System","Light","Dark","Scientists","Collect cogs and add famous scientists to your team. Your pick keeps you company while you solve.","Joined your team:","Team lead","Play engineering, live the formulas.","Courses","Start","Daily goal","{n} new questions unlocked!","Unlocks when {x} joins your team","Difficulty","{n} questions","Term card","Calculator","Use as answer","Engineering calculator","Arithmetic, powers, roots, \u03c0, brackets, trig (degrees), log and ln. Understands implied multiplication like 2\u03c0 or 3(4+1).","Basic","Easy","Medium","Upper-medium","Hard","Upper-hard","Very hard","Solve","How to use it, step by step","Which friction formula?","Common mistake","Where do the questions appear?","Every scientist on your team unlocks a 46-question pack. You meet those questions here:\n\n\u2022 The \u25b6 Solve button on the card: 10 questions from that pack\n\u2022 Play \u203a Daily questions: the 5 you have seen least from open packs\n\u2022 Play \u203a Bot duel: multiple-choice questions from open packs\n\u2022 Play \u203a Missions: story questions (locked ones show \ud83d\udd12)\n\u2022 Learn \u203a a formula \u203a Practice this\n\nDifficulty: Archimedes basic, Pascal easy, Torricelli medium, Newton upper-medium, Bernoulli hard, Euler upper-hard (estimation), Reynolds very hard.\n\nFormula count: Archimedes and Pascal questions use one formula, Torricelli and Newton 2\u20133, Bernoulli, Euler and Reynolds 4. Hard questions combine 2\u20133 topics (\ud83e\udde9 composite).\n\nTools \u203a Diagrams: solve questions with the Moody, pump-curve and viscosity charts.","Diagrams","Moody, pump curve, viscosity and flow regime. Solve questions on the chart.","Charts engineers use every day. Slide your finger across the chart and read the value.","{n} questions","{n} formulas","Composite","Formula chain","Diagram question","\ud83d\udcdd Solve with this diagram ({n})","How to read it","Tap the chart or slide your finger left and right.","\ud83d\udcc8 Open the diagram","Relative roughness \u03b5/D","smooth","Check with Colebrook","Pump curve","System curve","Operating point","Valve opening","Closing the valve steepens the system curve; the operating point slides left: less flow, more head.","water","air","Moody Chart","Friction factor f against Reynolds number and relative roughness (\u03b5/D).","Compute Re = V\xb7D/\u03bd and find it on the horizontal axis.","Take \u03b5 from the pipe material (e.g. cast iron 0.26 mm), compute \u03b5/D and pick that curve.","If Re < 2300, use the straight laminar line on the left (f = 64/Re), not a curve.","Read f to the left of where the curve meets your Re, then use it in Darcy\u2013Weisbach.","Pump and System Curve","How much can the pump deliver, how much does the system need? Where they cross is the operating point.","Pump curve (orange): the more flow, the less head the pump gives.","System curve (blue): static lift plus friction losses that grow with flow squared.","Where the curves cross is the flow and head the pump really runs at.","For power, put Q and H at the crossing into P = \u03c1\xb7g\xb7Q\xb7H/\u03b7.","Viscosity vs Temperature","How the kinematic viscosity of water and air changes with temperature.","Find the temperature on the horizontal axis.","The blue curve is water\u2019s \u03bd (left axis), the orange curve air\u2019s \u03bd (right axis).","Values are in mm\xb2/s: multiply by 10\u207b\u2076 for m\xb2/s.","Use this \u03bd in Re = V\xb7D/\u03bd to find the flow regime.","Flow Regime Map","Shows which friction formula to use for a given Re.","Re < 2300: laminar \u2192 f = 64/Re.","2300 \u2013 4000: transition, avoided in design.","Re > 4000, smooth pipe: Blasius. Rough pipe: Moody chart.","Curriculum","The {u} units and {n} formulas of the {c} course. Tap a unit to see its formulas.","Unit {n}","{f} formulas \xb7 {q} questions","My notes","New note","Note","Back to notes","Close","Delete","Jot down formulas, hints or solution steps here. You can reach them from every page.","Write your note\u2026 The first line becomes the title.","Saved automatically","Note deleted","Undo","Untitled note","Today","Learn engineering by playing","Measuring pressure","Computing flow","Checking Reynolds","Bernoulli ready","Tap to skip","Create your account","Appear on the leaderboard under your name. Your details stay on this device only.","First name","Last name","Email","Start","Enter your first name.","Enter your last name.","Enter a valid email (e.g. name@uni.edu).","Phone (optional)","Enter a valid phone number (e.g. +44 7700 900123) or leave it empty.","Welcome, {n}! \ud83c\udf93","Compete on the leaderboard by name","Your progress is saved","Your notes and badges stay with you","My account","Sign out","Sign out? Your progress stays on this device and continues when you sign in again.","Edit details","Save","Cancel","Exam Prep","Multi-stage problems of the kind set in university midterms and finals. Each exam has 4 problems.","Midterm Exams","Final Exams","Fluid properties, statics, buoyancy, rigid-body motion, Bernoulli, energy and momentum.","Basic concepts, energy, pure substances, closed and open systems, second law, entropy.","Exergy, power and refrigeration cycles, psychrometrics, combustion and compressible flow.","Conduction, thermal resistances, cylinders and spheres, fins, heat generation and transients.","Heat exchangers, forced and natural convection, condensation, boiling and radiation.","Dimensional analysis, pipe flow, pumps, cavitation, external flow, open channels and compressible flow.","Midterm {n}","Final {n}","4 problems \xb7 {p} parts","Best: {n}%","New","Watch an ad to enter","Exam ads left today: {n}/{m}","No exam ads left today. Come back tomorrow, or go ad-free with mecSI+.","Tip: mecSI+ makes exams and rewards ad-free and shields your streak (one-time purchase).","Enter the exam","Watch a short ad to open {e}. Afterwards the 4-problem exam opens.","\u25b6 Watch ad","Leave this round?","Privacy policy","Swipe to move between tabs","Skip","Next","Let\u2019s go","App tour","Welcome to mecSI","Learn engineering by playing. Fluid Mechanics, Thermodynamics and Heat Transfer in one app, and it works offline.","3 courses","200+ formula cards","Works offline","Learn","The syllabus unit by unit, and a card for every formula: what it\u2019s for, its symbols, an everyday example and common mistakes.","Formula cards","Diagrams","Unit by unit","Play, keep your streak","Solve 5 questions a day and grow your streak. Earn XP and cogs with missions, the error hunt and the robot duel; unlock new scientists with cogs.","5 a day","Robot duel","Error hunt","Get ready for exams","10 midterm and 10 final practice exams in every course. Multi-stage problems, step-by-step solutions and tables right inside the question.","60 practice exams","Step-by-step","Tables built in","Your tools, always at hand","Steam and air tables, an engineering calculator, a unit converter and a glossary. Swipe left and right to move between tabs.","Tables","Calculator","TR \xb7 EN \xb7 DE glossary","Swipe between tabs","Home page guide","Close","Back","Got it","Switching courses","Switch between Fluid Mechanics, Thermodynamics and Heat Transfer here. The course you pick changes the whole app: formulas, questions, exams, tables and terms all follow it. Your XP, streak and cogs are shared by every course.","Cogs, hints and theme","Cogs (\u2699) build up as you solve questions; spend them on scientists and hints. Bulbs (\ud83d\udca1) open a hint in a question. Tap either to go to the shop in Profile. The button on the far right switches light/dark theme.","Language","Use the app in Turkish, English or German. Questions, formulas and explanations switch too.","Today\u2019s task","Solve 5 questions a day; finishing the goal adds a day to your streak. Questions are picked from the ones you\u2019ve seen least.","Level and stats","Collect XP to level up; every new level gives +50 \u2699. Streak: days in a row. Today: your daily goal. Accuracy: your share of correct answers.","Quick start","Daily questions, real-life missions, the Error hunt where you find the mistake in a solution, and the Robot duel with 20-second questions. All use the selected course.","Midterm and final practice","10 midterms and 10 finals per course, with multi-stage problems. Enter by watching an ad, {n} times a day; with mecSI+ no ads and no limit.","Team leader\u2019s tip","Your team-leader scientist gives you tips; tap the card for a new one. Change your team leader in Profile.","Daily chest","Opens once a day with cogs and hints inside. A new chest arrives tomorrow.","Formula of the day","A formula from the selected course every day: its figure, the formula and an everyday example. Tap \u201cOpen\u201d for the full card.","Courses","You can switch course here too; the selected one has a tick. Locked ones are courses coming soon.","Tabs","Home, Learn, Play, Tools and Profile. Swipe left or right to change tabs too. The floating notebook on the edge lets you take notes on any page.","Pick up where you left off","Continue","{a}/{b} done","Questions are renewed every 2 weeks","New questions in {n} days","New questions arrive tomorrow","Add friend","Close","Give your code to a friend or type theirs. Once the request is accepted, you see each other on the leaderboard.","Your code","This code belongs to this phone and never changes.","Share code","Copied; send it via WhatsApp etc.","Your friend\u2019s code","Send request","Be my friend on mecSI! Type my code in Profile \u2192 Add friend: {c}","Request sent: {n}. They appear on your leaderboard once they accept.","You are now friends: {n}","You already sent a request; waiting for an answer.","You are already friends.","No student has this code. Check it again.","That is your own code.","A code has 8 characters (e.g. K7Q2-9XPD).","Could not connect. Check your internet connection.","Friend requests","{n} sent you a friend request","Accept","Decline","Requests you sent","waiting for an answer","Withdraw request","Your friends ({n})","Remove","Remove {n} from your friends?","Sign up first","Create a profile to add friends. Your friends see you on the leaderboard by name.","Create your profile first, then tap \u201cAdd friend\u201d to compete with friends.","No friends yet. Tap \u201cAdd friend\u201d, share your code or type your friend\u2019s code.","Friends are coming soon! Add friends and compete by name on the leaderboard.","Connecting\u2026","Could not load friends. Check your internet connection.","Try again","Friends see only your name, XP and streak. Your e-mail and phone are never shared.","Scores update live.","Friends","Global","you","More","Report and block","Report and block","Report {n} for an offensive name? They are removed from your list and can no longer send you requests.","Reported and blocked. Thank you!","Please enter an appropriate name.","Delete my account","Delete your account?","Your name, e-mail and phone are removed from this device; your friend record, code and requests are removed from the server. This cannot be undone.","Also delete my progress (XP, badges, streak)","Delete permanently","Could not delete. Check your internet connection and try again.","Your account was deleted.","Your progress in this round will not be saved.","Leave","Keep going","mecSI+ perks","No ads at all: ad-free exams and rewards, a streak shield and a gold profile.","No ads anywhere in the app (banners, interstitials and app-open ads are gone)","Tired of ads? mecSI+ removes them all.","Midterms and finals with no ads and no daily limit","Ad-free rewards: 2\xd7 XP and hints instantly","Streak shield: one missed day a week won\u2019t break your streak","Daily chest pays double cogs and hints","Gold profile frame and mecSI+ badge","Every course included; one-time payment, no subscription","Claim now: +3 \ud83d\udca1","Double your reward (no ad)","{n} ad-free rewards left today.","No rewards left today. They reset tomorrow.","Streak shield kicked in: your {n}-day streak is safe.","Streak shield ready","Streak shield used this week","mecSI+ \xb7 double reward","mecSI+ member","Cog & hint packs","Unlock more scientists and never get stuck. One-time purchase, no subscription.","Pocket Kit","Workshop Crate","Lab Vault","Most popular","Best value","Pack added: +{c} \u2699 and +{h} \ud83d\udca1","mecSI+ members get 50% more in every pack \u2192","You\u2019re a mecSI+ member: 50% more cogs and hints in every pack.","Packs are bought in the mecSI Android and iPhone app.","See packs","{n}% off","Discount compared with buying the same cogs as Pocket Kits.","{p} \xb7 Buy","Restore purchases","mecSI+ is bought in the Android and iPhone app (Google Play / App Store). The web version takes no payments.","The store can\u2019t be reached right now. Try again later.","mecSI+ active \xb7 all perks unlocked","Thank you! mecSI+ is unlocked.","The purchase could not be completed.","Go ad-free with mecSI+","one-time","Developer test: unlock mecSI+","mecSI+ restored.","No mecSI+ purchase found to restore on this Apple/Google account.","Test: switch mecSI+ off (to try buying again)","mecSI+ is off on this device. You can buy or restore it again.","Problems","Start the exam","Tip: each problem\u2019s parts (a), (b), (c) come in order; one part\u2019s result feeds the next. Calculator and hints are allowed.","Problem {p} ({x})","{n} parts","Suggested time: {n} min","Get ready for midterms and finals","20 practice exams \xb7 multi-stage problems","Fluid Mechanics, Thermodynamics and Heat Transfer are ready; more courses are on the way.","Heat Transfer","Not now","You can create your profile in Profile any time.","Create profile","Get on the leaderboard by name and keep your badges and progress.","Just a few details. Everything stays on this device and is never sent anywhere.","Update your details. Everything stays on this device.","Leaderboard","Badges","Progress","Create my profile","Notebook","Open your notes; brings the notebook back if hidden.","Hide notebook","Notebook hidden. Open it again with the \u201cNotebook\u201d button on a question.","Today\u2019s task","Start today\u2019s 5 questions","Keep going","Goal done! Keep practising if you like.","Solve your first questions; streak, accuracy and level will show here.","Background animation","Formulas drifting behind the pages","+{n} XP"],t.l)
